    "body": "Related, same Hub run (pr.nc lines 17-29): the first zig-zag ramp starts at Z0.0587 (G0 to Z0.0587, then the first arc to Z0.0538). The hole top is at Z-0.020 (#1558: 0.020 in below the stock top). At 3 deg, about 0.0049 in per arc, the tool makes ~16 back-and-forth arcs in air before it reaches material. When this issue is worked: start the first ramp a small clearance above the hole top (the top of material at the hole), not at the retract plane. The ramp angle in material stays the same.",
